      "id": 1,
      "text": "Milford Center was originally called Milford and was platted in Ohio in 1816.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milford_Center%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A post office opened as Milford in 1823, became Milford Centre in 1829, and settled on Milford Center in 1893.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milford_Center%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The village grew around the Big 4 Railroad, with a hotel that hosted salesmen from Columbus and livery services covering surrounding areas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofmilfordcenter.com/history.html",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1950s and 60s, downtown hosted two grocery stores, a hatchery, a shoe repair shop, a jewelry store, a restaurant, a doctor, a dentist, and four service stations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.villageofmilfordcenter.com/history.html",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "editorial_filler"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Today, Milford Center hosts a Church of Christ in Christian Union and a United Methodist Church, while former churches now serve other purposes.",
